Two test classes, both against the same PostgreSQL database, each with this in its constructor:

```csharp
public TicketQueryTests()
{
    _db = TestContext.Create();
    _db.Database.ExecuteSqlRaw("TRUNCATE \"Tickets\", \"Comments\" CASCADE");
    Seed.Tickets(_db);
}
```

Run on their own, both classes pass. Run together, between 3 and 14 tests fail, and a different set each time. Running any single failing test alone passes.

What is happening, and which fix removes the failure mode rather than hiding it?

solution.code:
function fixtureCollisions(tests) {
  const owners = new Map();
  for (const test of tests) {
    const unique = new Set(test.fixtureIds);
    for (const id of unique) {
      const names = owners.get(id) ?? [];
      names.push(test.name);
      owners.set(id, names);
    }
  }

  const collisions = [];
  for (const [id, names] of owners) {
    if (names.length > 1) collisions.push(id);
  }
  return collisions.sort();
}

